cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use BeyondNN in your research, please cite the software as below."
type: software
title: "BeyondNN: auditable interpretability evidence for PyTorch"
abstract: >-
  BeyondNN turns claims about neural-network computation into structured,
  provenance-aware, testable objects and audits them against recorded evidence:
  epistemic status for every record, declared claims, controlled interventions with
  explicit replacements, configuration roles, and deterministic, re-derivable audits
  without a global score.
authors:
  - family-names: Roufas
    given-names: Nikolaos
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-01"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/NikolasRoufas/beyondnn"
url: "https://github.com/NikolasRoufas/beyondnn"
keywords:
  - interpretability
  - pytorch
  - mechanistic interpretability
  - provenance
  - causal interventions
  - research software
